 "ran": "A probe agent with no effort, under --effort low, project effortLevel low, CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL low, nothing set, a user top-level low on a Fable 5.1 main session, and a user modelSettings low for the main model only; a probe agent with effort high under --effort low, project low and CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL low.",
 "result": "With no effort, the agent ran at --effort, the project key or the variable (low), and at its own model's default when nothing applied to its model: Fable 5.1 sent high under a medium main session, and Haiku 5.5 sent medium when the low came from the user top-level key (ignored on Haiku 5.5) or from a modelSettings entry for the main model. So the agent resolves effort for its own model; a level that counts only for the main model doesn't carry over. Frontmatter high beat --effort low and project low. CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL low beat frontmatter high.",
 "method": "dashboard/experiments/harness: claude -p in a throwaway HOME, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and project under $TMPDIR, a fake key and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL on 127.0.0.1. fakeapi.py logs the model, output_config.effort and cache_control ttl of each request. It answers 400, or a short text reply when the case sets text_reply; for agent cases it first streams one Agent tool call. Cases with prompt \"/effort status\" record the command's output, and runcase.py reads the effort fields from the throwaway transcripts before deleting them. The harness only allows requests to fakeapi.py on 127.0.0.1. Managed settings were not tested, because writing them needs admin rights.",
